{"role":"user","message":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<timestamp>Monday, Oct 5, 2026, 7:27 PM (UTC+5:30)</timestamp>\n<user_query>\nYou are the code-writing delegate for one feature. You own the git worktree at D:\\Experiments\\rstackexp-wt\\task-tracker exclusively (branch feat/task-tracker, already checked out, based on main, currently clean with no index.html). Nobody else writes there while you run. Do all work inside that worktree. Do not touch D:\\Experiments\\rstackexp. Do not push. Do not open a PR. Shell is Windows PowerShell 5, so separate commands with `;` not `&&`.\n\n## Deliverable\n\nCreate exactly one new file, `index.html`, at the worktree root. A single-page task tracker. Vanilla JS, inline `<style>` and `<script>`, no build step, no dependencies, no external requests (no CDN, no fonts). It must work opened as file:// and when served from localhost.\n\nUser-facing behavior:\n- Add a task by typing a title and pressing Enter or clicking Add. Whitespace-only titles are ignored. Input clears after add.\n- Edit a task's title inline. Clicking its Edit button swaps the title for a text input prefilled with the title and focused. Enter or blur saves. Escape cancels. A trimmed-empty title on save keeps the old title.\n- Toggle done / not done with a checkbox. Done tasks render with a line-through title.\n- Delete a task with its Delete button. No confirm dialog.\n- Tasks persist in localStorage and survive reload. Order is insertion order.\n- Empty list shows a one-line hint such as \"No tasks yet.\"\n\n## Data shape (decided, do not change)\n\n```js\n// Task = { id: string, title: string, done: boolean }\n// tasks: Task[]          persisted under localStorage key 'tasks' as JSON\n// editingId: string|null  UI-only, never persisted; at most one row edits at a time\n```\n\nOrganizing structure: one source of truth, the `tasks` array. Every mutation is a small pure function that returns a new array (`addTask`, `renameTask`, `toggleTask`, `removeTask`), and every mutation flows through one `commit(nextTasks)` that assigns, saves to localStorage, and re-renders. Render is a full re-render of the list from `tasks` + `editingId`; the DOM is never the source of truth. `load()` is the only boundary guard: parse localStorage, and if the result is not an array of objects with string id, string title, boolean done, fall back to `[]`. No other validation anywhere. Ids come from `crypto.randomUUID()`. Event handling via one delegated listener on the list element plus one submit handler on the add form, dispatching on `data-action` attributes, not per-row listeners.\n\n## DOM contract (I will drive this in a browser, keep these exact)\n\n- `<form id=\"add-form\">` containing `<input id=\"new-task\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"What needs doing?\" autocomplete=\"off\">` and `<button type=\"submit\">Add</button>`.\n- `<ul id=\"tasks\">`. Each task is `<li data-id=\"...\" class=\"task\">` (add class `done` when done) containing, in order: `<input type=\"checkbox\" data-action=\"toggle\">`, then either `<span class=\"title\">` or, when editing, `<input type=\"text\" class=\"edit\" data-action=\"edit-input\">`, then `<button data-action=\"edit\">Edit</button>`, `<button data-action=\"delete\">Delete</button>`.\n- `<p id=\"empty\">No tasks yet.</p>` shown only when the list is empty.\n\nStyling: minimal, clean, readable, system font stack, centered column max-width ~32rem, a little spacing. Nothing fancy, no animations, under ~40 lines of CSS.\n\n## Code rules\n\n- Keep the file small, target 120 to 180 lines total. Flat functions at script top level, no classes, no IIFE wrappers, no framework-like abstractions.\n- Comments: keep only a non-obvious *why* the code cannot show. No section banners, no restating what a line does. The three-line data-shape comment above is fine to keep as the single comment at the top of the script.\n- Use `textContent`, never innerHTML with user text.\n- No console.log left behind.\n\n## Verify before you return\n\nWrite the file, then check it parses by extracting the script and running `node --check` on it, or by loading it once in the Cursor built-in browser (cursor-ide-browser MCP `browser_navigate` to the file:// URL) and confirming no console errors. One check is enough; the parent runs the full add/edit/toggle/delete/reload drive in the browser.\n\nCommit once on feat/task-tracker with message `feat(tracker): add single-page task tracker in index.html` and no body.\n\n## Return to me\n\n1. The commit SHA and `git status --short` of the worktree (must be clean).\n2. Line count of index.html.\n3. Which check you ran and its result.\n4. Any point where you deviated from this brief and why. Keep the report under 25 lines.\n</user_query>"}]}}
